##
 * vir/crypto/aes.vri — AES-128/256 Block Cipher + GCM Mode
 * ===========================================================
 * Inspired by NIST FIPS 197 (AES) + NIST SP 800-38D (GCM)
 * Inspired by Go: crypto/aes, crypto/cipher
 * Inspired by Rust: aes, aes-gcm crates
 *
 * Phase C — symmetric encryption for data protection.
 * Implements AES-128 and AES-256 in ECB, CTR, and GCM modes.
 * GCM provides authenticated encryption (AEAD).
 *
 * ⚠️ SECURITY NOTE
 * The S-Box lookup in _aes_sub_bytes uses table indexing which is
 * vulnerable to cache-timing side-channel attacks. For local-attacker
 * threat models, prefer hardware AES-NI via aes_encrypt_block_hw()
 * which uses constant-time CPU instructions.
 *
 * WARNING: ECB mode is insecure for most uses. Prefer GCM.
 ##

include types;
include result;
import Result, Ok, Err from result;
include string;
import String, str_new from string;
include vec;
import Vec, vec_new, vec_push, vec_len, vec_get from vec;
include copy;
import mem_copy, mem_set from copy;

